<h1>Stilt, in <em>one</em> page</h1>
<p>Stilt checks every <strong>effect</strong> a function performs, and the
compiler infers the rest.<br />
A line that ends with two spaces breaks.</p>
<h2>What it gives</h2>
<ul>
<li>Values that are copied, never shared</li>
<li>Errors in types: <code>raise&lt;E&gt;</code> and <code>try</code>
<ul>
<li>every raising call is marked</li>
<li>a catch-all needs a reason</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Fast builds, with <a href="https://cranelift.dev" title="the code generator">Cranelift</a></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Write the code.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Run <code>stilt check</code>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Read the diagnostics.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>Each name has one home.
A reader finds it by its qualifier,
and so does a tool.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<pre><code class="language-stilt">fn main() / io { print(&quot;1 &lt; 2 &amp;&amp; 3 &gt; 2&quot;) }
</code></pre>
<p>Escapes: *not emphasis*, <code>a ` tick</code>, snake_case_name, 2 * 3 * 4, and <a href="https://stilt.dev">https://stilt.dev</a>.</p>
